# Deploy approval: {service} {version}

`{service}` version `{version}` is ready for production. This document was
generated by the release agent. Approving fires the `deploy.approve`
capability declared in the manifest below. The document cannot define what
that capability does; the host grants it, or it does not run.

```ad-state
service: "checkout-service"
version: "2.4.1"
approved: false
decision: "awaiting review"
approver: ""
note: ""
```

```ad-manifest
name: deploy.approve
min-version: 1.0.0
scopes: ["deploy:write", "audit:write"]
```

```ad-manifest
name: deploy.reject
min-version: 1.0.0
scopes: ["audit:write"]
```

## Change summary

The release contains 7 files changed across 3 commits:

| area | change | risk |
|---|---|---|
| payments | retry policy for declined cards | medium |
| cart | latency fix on session lookup | low |
| infra | base image bumped to node:22 | low |

The reviewer note below travels with the decision into the audit log.

```ad-action?name=deploy.approve&role=primary&when=!approved
id: approve
on:click: cap.send("deploy.approve", {version: version, approver: approver, note: note})
---
Approve deploy ({version})
```

```ad-action?name=deploy.reject&role=danger&when=!approved
id: reject
on:click: cap.send("deploy.reject", {version: version, approver: approver, note: note})
---
Reject and reopen
```

